      "heading": "What Is Gluco Care Natural Diabetes Supplement and How Does It Affect Blood Sugar?",
      "body": "<p>Gluco Care is a dietary supplement combining vitamins, minerals, and a wide blend of botanical extracts marketed for blood sugar support. Based on the product's own Supplement Facts label, the formula includes both foundational nutrients and a proprietary herbal blend rather than a single headline compound.</p>\n<h4 class=\"tbl-title\">Vitamins &amp; Minerals (Per Label)</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"md-table\"><thead><tr><th class=\"tbl-th\">Ingredient</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Amount</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Vitamin C</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Antioxidant; supports blood vessel health</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Vitamin E</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">10 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Fat-soluble antioxidant</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Magnesium</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">125 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Cofactor for insulin action</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Zinc</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">7.5 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Supports insulin storage and secretion</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Manganese</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">1 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Involved in carbohydrate metabolism</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote><p><strong>Label Discrepancy Worth Flagging:</strong> the label lists Chromium at 67&nbsp;mg. The typical daily value for chromium is roughly 35&nbsp;mcg (micrograms) — 67&nbsp;mg would be about 1,900 times that amount. This is almost certainly a labeling unit error (mg written where mcg was meant), but we can't confirm that without the manufacturer. If you have this product, it's worth verifying the actual chromium dose with them directly before use, particularly if you take other supplements or medications.</p></blockquote>\n<h4 class=\"tbl-title\">Botanical Blend (Per Label)</h4>\n<div class=\"tbl-wrap\"><table class=\"md-table\"><thead><tr><th class=\"tbl-th\">Ingredient</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Amount</th><th class=\"tbl-th\">Traditional / Studied Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Gymnema sylvestre (leaf)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Most-studied ingredient in this blend for glucose support</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Bitter melon (fruit extract)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Traditional glucose-support botanical; evidence is mixed</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Cinnamon (bark)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Studied for modest insulin-sensitivity effects</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Banaba (leaf, 1% corosolic acid)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">25 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Standardized extract; limited human trial data</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">White mulberry (leaf)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">25 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Contains DNJ, studied for slowing carb absorption</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Guggul (resin)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Traditionally used for cholesterol; weaker glucose data</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Licorice (root)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">50 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Anti-inflammatory; whole-root licorice can raise blood pressure at high intake</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Alpha-Lipoic Acid</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">30 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Antioxidant; clinical trials typically use 300–600 mg, well above this amount</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Vanadium (as vanadyl sulfate)</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">0.2 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Mixed human data; studied doses are typically 10–30 mg</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-odd\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Taurine</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">25 mg</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Amino acid studied for beta-cell protection</td></tr><tr class=\"tbl-row-even\"><td class=\"tbl-td\">Cayenne, Yarrow, Juniper Berry</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">10–25 mg each</td><td class=\"tbl-td\">Traditional inclusions; limited modern glucose-specific evidence</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Worth Noting on Dosing</h3>\n<p>Two ingredients stand out as dosed well below the amounts typically used in clinical research: alpha-lipoic acid (30 mg here vs. 300–600 mg in most trials) and vanadium (0.2 mg here vs. 10–30 mg in studied doses). That doesn't make them useless — smaller amounts within a broader blend can still contribute — but it does mean the clinical evidence for those specific compounds at high doses doesn't necessarily translate to what's actually in this product.</p>\n<p><strong>Action Tip</strong>: Compare the label above against the current bottle before purchasing — supplement formulas can change between production runs.</p>\n",
